entry='<article class="paper-row" id="preparation-certificate-v01"><div class="paper-number">G19</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Certifying preparation without choosing a gauge</h2><p>Twenty-seven invariant scalars give a constructive upper bound on distance to the critical orbit.</p><p class="muted">A spanning tree combines transported matter coherence, full cycle holonomies and electric energy. The score vanishes exactly on the reference orbit and has explicit local conditioning. Guaranteed interval inputs can certify entry into the frozen endpoint trapping ball. Exact zero-Gauss counterexamples show why active dressed loops alone cannot certify full preparation, even from their complete history at rank at least two. Forty-six exact checks and finite-rank floating diagnostics pass. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0. Precision budgets are sufficient mathematical bounds without laboratory calibration.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="'+link+files[2]+'">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="'+link+z.name+'">Proof and measurement contract ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GPC01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article>'
