p=R/'dist/updates/index.html';t=p.read_text();assert 'preparation-certificate-v01' not in t
entry='<article class="claim" id="preparation-certificate-v01"><div class="eyebrow">18 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>Preparation now has a gauge-invariant sufficient certificate</h2><p>A global orbit-distance upper score combines 27 real invariant inputs. Exact rational enclosures can establish entry into the previous endpoint trapping ball, with no prior local-chart assumption. Norm/Gauss validity, measurement coverage and model-error bounds remain separate inputs.</p><p>The eight-page theorem also proves an obstruction: configuration-only observations miss arbitrary admissible electric circulation, and active loop histories miss independent unused-color dynamics at rank ≥2. The exact calculator, 46 finite-topology/rational checks and numerical matrix controls are available. The conservative unit raw-interval allocation is about 2.93×10⁻⁴³ in model units, a sufficient bound rather than a physical precision requirement. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#preparation-certificate-v01">Read the preparation theorem →</a></article>'
